# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Order matters: `.env*` is ignored wholesale, then the example files are taken
# back out. Putting `!.env.example` BEFORE the broad rule does not work, because
# git refuses to re-include a file inside a directory it has already excluded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Credentials that have no business being committed under any name.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
id_rsa
id_ed255519
credentials.json
service-account*.json

